WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.100
In the MCU, everyone's favorite foul-mouthed,&nbsp;
trigger-happy rodent has always been known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:11.385
"Rocket." But where did he get his name? And what&nbsp;
species is he really? Warning! Spoilers ahead!

00:00:11.385 --> 00:00:16.140
As the last movie in James Gunn's trilogy of&nbsp;
sci-fi epics, "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.760
3" sends off its team of misfits in high&nbsp;
fashion. Rather than saving the universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.020
this time around the gang is on a mission&nbsp;
to save Rocket's life. But to do so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.380
they'll have to scour their friend's&nbsp;
past and find a way to bypass a kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.480
switch activated inside of him. As the story&nbsp;
unfolds, the audience is treated to flashbacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.740
of Rocket's origins. In them, we learn how he&nbsp;
was experimented on by the High Evolutionary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.340
to become the hyper-intelligent,&nbsp;
jaded rodent we all know and love.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.440
Audiences get to see Rocket go from a baby raccoon&nbsp;
to a creature learning the basics of science,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.820
all the way to innovating on the High&nbsp;
Evolutionary's processes. And naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.380
there's a point where the audience learns where&nbsp;
Rocket got his namesake. As the High Evolutionary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.180
teaches Rocket, the little mammal sees a ship take&nbsp;
off and correctly identifies it as a "rocket."

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.200
Later, when Rocket and his cohorts are in&nbsp;
their cages, they discuss naming themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.880
This is a small act of rebellion against the&nbsp;
High Evolutionary and the designations he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.040
given them. Rocket's friends name themselves&nbsp;
Lylla, Teefs, and Floor. When it's Rocket's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.060
turn he recalls how he has always dreamt&nbsp;
of going into the sky and remembers the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.040
ship escaping the power of gravity. In that&nbsp;
fateful moment, he gives himself his true name.

00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:26.700
Given his tragic upbringing, it's&nbsp;
no surprise that Rocket is deeply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.600
insecure about his body and his place&nbsp;
in the world. He has a long history of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.620
getting offended when people refer to him as&nbsp;
an animal. He's been called everything from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.600
a rabbit to a badger. Peter Quill calls him a&nbsp;
raccoon, an animal Rocket has never heard of.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.860
"What's a raccoon?"

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.140
"What's a raccoon? It's what you are, stupid."

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:45.999
"Ain't no thing like me, 'cept me."

00:01:45.999 --> 00:01:50.640
Each time he's compared to an animal, Rocket&nbsp;
explodes in anger. He's always viewed himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.040
as one-of-a-kind, so being compared to a rodent or&nbsp;
a critter is perhaps the greatest insult to him.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.120
However, Rocket's sense of self is challenged&nbsp;
when he finds a lab on the High Evolutionary's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.760
ship housing other animals, including a cage&nbsp;
of baby raccoons. As Rocket opens the cage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.360
and the babies quickly flock to&nbsp;
him he sees a label. And it's at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.480
that moment that Rocket learns what&nbsp;
he's been all along — a raccoon.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.860
In the comics, "Rocket" has always been&nbsp;
"Rocket Raccoon," but explaining his species&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.880
in the movies has been on the back burner&nbsp;
in the MCU where he's only been referred to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.080
as "Rocket." That changes during his final&nbsp;
confrontation with the High Evolutionary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:30.060
as Rocket lets him know once and for all that he's&nbsp;
not just an experiment. He's "Rocket Raccoon."

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.440
It's a celebratory moment where Rocket&nbsp;
fully embraces who he is. He's spent a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.040
lifetime running away from his past and&nbsp;
the painful memories that lurk there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.780
But with one defiant statement, he makes it&nbsp;
clear that the High Evolutionary no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.740
controls him. Rocket's calling the shots&nbsp;
from now on, and he has his family to back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.400
him up. With their help, Rocket takes&nbsp;
on the High Evolutionary one last time.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.620
Rocket is indeed a raccoon, and it's nothing for&nbsp;
him to be ashamed of. After all the trauma and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.120
abuse he endured, he's finally come to accept&nbsp;
where he's from. This newfound sense of place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.167
and identity allows him to move on as the&nbsp;
new captain of the Guardians of the Galaxy.

